# Candidate coordinates for the marked icosian comparison

These rational matrices and integer coefficient tables specify an explicit
candidate comparison. They are DATA, not an asserted lattice isometry.
The comparison proof must verify inverse identities, the form identity,
both integral containments, and right rational-quaternion linearity.

The tables were obtained by matching quaternion Gram frames in the actual
Golay Leech lattice. The existing marked coordinate and source-generator
conventions are those of Gerald Höhn's attributed ATLAS icosian ports.
The source six-dimensional Gram matrix is John Bray's `6L34G1-Ar6aB0`.
Reproducible searches and exact arithmetic checks are retained in
`Scratch/LeechBlockRealization/find_comparison.py` and
`complete_comparison_data.py`; those checks are not Lean proofs.
-/

